SA-MP 0.3 Server Setup
----------------------

Once the configuration is complete, run> ./samp03svr & to start the server process.

CONFIGURATION:

Example server.cfg:
	echo Executing Server Config...
	lanmode 0
	maxplayers 32
	port 7777
	hostname Unnamed Server
	announce 0
	gamemode0 lvdm 1
	gamemode1 rivershell 1
	weburl www.sa-mp.com
	rcon_password changeme

To configure the server, you must edit the values in server.cfg. They 
are explained below:

hostname
--------
	Parameters:
		string
	
	Description:
		Specifies the hostname shown in the server browser
		
port
----
	Parameters:
		int
	
	Description:
		Specifies the port to listen on.
		This port is used for game connections, rcon 
connections, and for querying.
	
maxplayers
----------
	Parameters:
		int
	
	Description:
		Specifies the maximum amount of players.
		
lanmode
-------
	Parameters:
		int (0 or 1)
		
	Description:
		Turns lanmode on (1) or off (0). Lanmode (as the name 
suggests) is for use on LAN games, where bandwidth is not a problem. 
Lanmode sends data at a higher rate, for a smoother game.
		

announce
-------
	Parameters:
		int (0 or 1)
		
	Description:
		Announces your server to the 'Internet' server list in 
the SA:MP browser. On (1) or Off (0).

weburl
------
	Parameters:
		string
	
	Description:
		Specifies the URL shown in the server browser, which is 
associated to the server.
		
rcon_password
-------------
	Parameters:
		string
		
	Description:
		Specifies the password needed to connect to rcon, or 
login to rcon ingame.
		
gamemode0 - gamemode15
----------------------
	Parameters:
		string
		int
		
	Description:
		Specifies the rotation settings. The first parameter 
sets the game mode name. The second is the number of times it will 
repeat.
		You can use gamemode0 to specify the first gamemode, 
gamemode1 to specify the second, etc.


================================================================================
 PINECREST .env CONFIGURATION (multi-server)
================================================================================

The gamemode reads its runtime settings from an environment file so the same
compiled gamemode can run on several servers (different database, name, id)
without editing the Pawn source.

LOCATION
--------
	scriptfiles/.env

	SA-MP's Pawn file functions are sandboxed to the scriptfiles/ folder,
	so the file MUST live there. A template is provided:

		cp scriptfiles/.env.example scriptfiles/.env

	The file is read once in OnGameModeInit() by
	gamemodes/logic/server_config.inc. If the file (or a single key) is
	missing, the built-in defaults are used, so the server still starts.

FORMAT
------
	KEY=VALUE, one per line. Lines starting with '#' are comments.
	Surrounding single/double quotes around a value are stripped.

VARIABLES
---------
	MYSQL_HOST
		MySQL server address.            Default: 127.0.0.1

	MYSQL_USER
		MySQL user name.                 Default: pinecrestphp

	MYSQL_PASSWORD
		MySQL password.                  Default: (built-in)

	MYSQL_DATABASE
		MySQL database name.             Default: pinecrestphp

	SERVER_NAME
		Gamemode text / browser hostname shown in the SA-MP server list.
		                                 Default: Pinecrest RolePlay

	SERVER_ID
		Logical id of this server instance, used across the gamemode to
		branch per-server behaviour.
			-1  = auto-detect from the "port" value in server.cfg
			 0  = main server, 1, 2, ... = additional servers
		                                 Default: -1 (auto)

NOTE ON PORT
------------
	The game listen "port" stays in server.cfg, because the SA-MP server
	binary needs it before the gamemode runs. SERVER_ID in .env lets you
	give each instance a stable id independent of its port.

EXAMPLE (second server)
-----------------------
	MYSQL_HOST=127.0.0.1
	MYSQL_USER=pinecrest2
	MYSQL_PASSWORD=secret
	MYSQL_DATABASE=pinecrest2
	SERVER_NAME=Pinecrest RolePlay #2
	SERVER_ID=1
